    "updated_at": "2023-12-04T08:52:48Z",
    "body": "Hello dtchang,\r\nthanks for your example (I think the issue is not from our code).\r\nIf you want to initialize the Executor from an Estimator, you have to initialize the Estimator as well.\r\nsession = Session(service, backend=service.get_backend(\"ibm_brisbane\"), max_time=28800)\r\nexecutor = Executor(Estimator(session))\r\nAs an alternative, you can also parse the initialized session to the Executor:\r\nsession = Session(service, backend=service.get_backend(\"ibm_brisbane\"), max_time=28800)\r\nexecutor = Executor(session)\r\nI think that should fix it! ",
